# snag-trace.log — t(sec) event fields
# wall_hit / wall_scrub: side contact (ny = normal.y, |ny|<0.5 means wall)
# speed_drop: flat speed fell >15% in one physics step while grounded
# corner: the slock's front crossed into a tile where a side wall starts or ends (L/R: W wall, F floor, V void,
#         before>after); drift = off the rail centre line; spd = speed this step
# raw_contact: contact as PhysX made it, BEFORE squaring, that pushes along the rail (ccd = continuous sweep)
# rail_turn: axis switch; carried = speed taken round the corner, from = speed before
